H("697.d.1.A",3,"A GIS student opens mapping software, saves a file in a folder and emails the map to a classmate. These tasks use:","operating systems, applications and networking tools together",["only a printer","only a calculator","no software at all"],"GIS work blends OS, application and network skills.")
H("697.d.1.A",4,"Before sharing a large map file with a team, a GIS technician should confirm that:","the recipients can open the file with their software and network access",["the file has no name","the file is deleted afterward","the screen is dimmed"],"Tools must work for every user.")
H("697.d.1.B",3,"In a GIS workstation, a digitizing tablet or scanner is an example of a(n):","input device",["output device","storage battery","network cable"],"Tablets and scanners bring data in.")
H("697.d.1.B",4,"A plotter that prints a large map is best described as a(n):","output device",["input device","processing chip","memory slot"],"Plotters produce printed output.")
H("697.d.1.C",3,"A team picks a mapping program by checking whether it can do the needed analysis, fits the budget and is reliable. They are:","evaluating software quality and appropriateness",["deleting files","naming layers","painting maps"],"Software is chosen against project needs.")
H("697.d.1.C",4,"Which factor matters most when selecting GIS software for a county water project?","Whether it can handle the needed spatial data and analysis",["The color of the box","The name of the company founder","The number of icons on the desktop"],"Capability for the task comes first.")
H("697.d.1.D",3,"A map layer saved in one format will not open in a second program. The technician should:","convert the file to a compatible format",["delete the layer","retype every point by hand","buy a new monitor"],"Format conversion solves compatibility issues.")
H("697.d.1.D",4,"A shapefile works on a Windows laptop but a coworker on another platform cannot open it. The first thing to check is:","cross-platform format and software compatibility",["screen resolution","keyboard layout","desk size"],"Compatibility issues are about formats and software.")
H("697.d.2.A",3,"A student uses a digital camera, a scanner and a GPS receiver to collect map data. These are:","input devices",["output devices only","storage racks","display stands"],"They bring data into the project.")
H("697.d.2.A",4,"Adding a GPS-tagged photo to a map product shows the use of:","an input device feeding a final product",["a printer jam","a lost password","a power outage"],"Inputs are incorporated into products.")
H("697.d.2.B",3,"Using the correct finger placement on home-row keys follows:","keyboarding standards",["a map legend","a coordinate grid","a license"],"Proper technique supports accurate data entry.")
H("697.d.2.B",4,"Accurate data entry matters in GIS because a mistyped coordinate can:","place a feature in the wrong location",["improve the map","speed up the printer","change the legend font"],"Small typos create large location errors.")
H("697.d.3.A",3,"Early thematic mapping, such as John Snow's cholera map, is an example of:","a historical use of mapping to find patterns",["a GPS satellite","a smartphone app","a drone camera"],"Mapped data revealed patterns in the past.")
H("697.d.3.A",4,"A contemporary development that makes GIS data easy to share is:","web-based mapping platforms",["paper-only atlases","hand-drawn charts","typewriters"],"Web mapping expanded access.")
H("697.d.3.B",3,"Which is a basic component of a GIS?","hardware, software and data",["paint, glue and string","pens, rulers and chalk","chairs, desks and shelves"],"GIS rests on hardware, software, data and people.")
H("697.d.3.B",4,"In a GIS, the people component includes:","analysts who manage, run and interpret the system",["only the monitor","only the map paper","only the keyboard"],"People operate and apply the GIS.")
H("697.d.3.C",3,"A city planner uses GIS to decide where to put a new fire station. This shows GIS used in:","public safety and planning careers",["music production","fashion design","bakery sales"],"GIS supports location decisions.")
H("697.d.3.C",4,"A farmer uses GIS and soil maps to adjust fertilizer across fields. This is an example of GIS in:","agriculture",["film editing","retail clothing","banking only"],"Precision agriculture relies on spatial data.")
H("697.d.4.A",3,"In a relational database built from a geographic data model, each map feature is linked to:","a table row of attributes",["a paper file","a coin","a color wheel"],"Attributes are stored in tables.")
H("697.d.4.A",4,"A geographic data model for roads might include attributes such as:","name, length and speed limit",["lunch menu","paint color of the sky","student grades"],"Attributes describe features.")
H("697.d.4.B",3,"A join in a database combines two tables using:","a field they share",["a random number","the printer name","the screen size"],"Joins match records on a common field.")
H("697.d.4.B",4,"Clicking a hyperlink field on a map feature to open its inspection report shows the use of:","hyperlinks within a database",["a sorting error","a battery drain","a projection"],"Hyperlinks connect features to related documents.")
H("697.d.4.C",3,"Grouping population values into ranges such as low, medium and high for a map is called:","classification",["deletion","encryption","scaling a font"],"Classification groups data into classes.")
H("697.d.4.C",4,"A mapmaker splits rainfall data into five classes with equal value ranges. This is the:","equal interval classification method",["random method","alphabet method","backup method"],"Equal interval uses same-width ranges.")
H("697.d.4.D",3,"Importing a spreadsheet of addresses into a GIS database is an example of:","transferring data from another source into a database",["printing a map","erasing a layer","changing a legend"],"Data can be imported from many sources.")
H("697.d.4.D",4,"Before importing a spreadsheet into a GIS database, a technician should:","check that columns and data types match what the database expects",["delete all headers","rename the file to a number only","turn off the computer"],"Clean, matching data imports correctly.")
H("697.d.5.A",3,"A satellite image downloaded from a government site is an example of a:","spatial data source",["recipe card","music file","phone bill"],"Imagery is a common spatial source.")
H("697.d.5.A",4,"Which source is a digital spatial database commonly used in GIS?","A county's online parcel and road layers",["A grocery receipt","A weather vane","A school lunch menu"],"Public agencies publish spatial layers.")
H("697.d.5.B",3,"Using GIS to find all schools within one mile of a highway is an example of:","spatial analysis",["word processing","file renaming","slide design"],"Spatial analysis answers location questions.")
H("697.d.5.B",4,"Spatial analysis is used appropriately when a planner wants to:","identify where a flood zone overlaps with homes",["spell check a letter","sort an email inbox","edit a video"],"Overlay analysis reveals relationships between locations.")
H("697.d.6.A",3,"A GIS technician needs to measure the distance between two points on a map. They should choose the:","measurement tool",["print preview","font menu","spell checker"],"Pick the tool that does the task.")
H("697.d.6.A",4,"For combining a flood layer with a parcel layer to find affected lots, the best tool is:","an overlay tool",["a text box","a color picker","a screen saver"],"Overlay tools combine layers.")
H("697.d.6.B",3,"A query that selects all parcels larger than five acres is an example of:","an attribute query",["a battery check","a printing job","a font change"],"Attribute queries select by data values.")
H("697.d.6.B",4,"A spatial query that finds all features within a boundary uses the:","location relationship between features and the boundary",["alphabet order of names","file size","screen brightness"],"Spatial queries use position and shape.")
H("697.d.6.C",3,"Mapmakers use a map projection when they need to:","show the curved Earth on a flat surface",["delete data","print only text","change file names"],"Projections flatten the globe.")
H("697.d.6.C",4,"Every map projection distorts something, so a mapmaker chooses one that:","preserves the property most important to the map's purpose",["makes the map blurry","removes all labels","hides the legend"],"Different projections preserve shape, area or distance.")
H("697.d.6.D",3,"Latitude and longitude are used to describe:","a location's coordinates on Earth",["a printer setting","a file size","a paint color"],"Coordinates pinpoint places.")
H("697.d.6.D",4,"A map scale of 1:24,000 means one unit on the map equals:","24,000 of the same units on the ground",["24 units on the ground","1,000 units on the ground","240 units on the ground"],"Scale ratios compare map to ground distance.")
H("697.d.7.A",3,"Before a class GPS data collection trip, a supervisor should:","plan the route, safety rules and tasks",["leave without a plan","skip all instructions","bring no equipment"],"Supervised experiences are planned.")
H("697.d.7.A",4,"A safe GPS field experience for students includes:","adult supervision and a clear plan for the area",["working alone at night","entering restricted areas","ignoring weather"],"Safety and supervision come first.")
H("697.d.7.B",3,"Before collecting points, a GPS receiver should be:","turned on and given time to lock onto satellites",["covered in a bag","turned off","held upside down in a closed box"],"Receivers need a satellite fix.")
H("697.d.7.B",4,"A technician sets the receiver's coordinate system and data format before collecting. This step is part of:","initializing and preparing the receiver",["printing the map","closing the project","deleting waypoints"],"Settings must match the project.")
H("697.d.7.C",3,"A GPS receiver records a location as:","coordinates such as latitude and longitude",["a recipe","a paragraph","a song"],"GPS reports coordinates.")
H("697.d.7.C",4,"To get the best accuracy when collecting a point, the user should:","hold still in an open area with a clear view of the sky",["stand under a thick roof","move quickly while recording","cover the antenna"],"Clear sky view improves the fix.")
H("697.d.7.D",3,"After the field work, the saved points on the GPS unit are:","downloaded to a personal computer",["thrown away","spoken aloud","painted on paper"],"Data is transferred for processing.")
H("697.d.7.D",4,"A common way to move GPS data to a computer is with:","a USB cable or wireless transfer and the manufacturer's software",["a pencil","a fax","a rubber band"],"Standard tools transfer the files.")
H("697.d.8.A",3,"A student collects text notes, photos, audio and video clips for a GIS project. This is:","gathering electronic information in various formats",["deleting files","erasing layers","printing blank paper"],"Multiple formats enrich a project.")
H("697.d.8.A",4,"When collecting electronic information for a GIS project, it is best to:","record the source and date of each item",["skip the source","use only memory","rename everything with one letter"],"Documented sources support credibility.")
H("697.d.8.B",3,"Authentic data for a GIS project comes from:","reliable electronic sources such as government agencies",["random rumors","unsigned posts with no source","guesses"],"Authentic data is traceable and reliable.")
H("697.d.8.B",4,"Before using data from a website in a map, a student should check that it is:","from a credible source and up to date",["the longest page","the most colorful","the first search result"],"Credibility and currency matter.")
H("697.d.9.A",3,"Project management for a GIS project includes setting goals, tasks and:","a timeline",["a lunch menu","a color theme only","a random password"],"Management guidelines include planning.")
H("697.d.9.A",4,"A GIS project team lists tasks, assigns people and sets deadlines. This is:","applying project management guidelines",["skipping the plan","ending the project","losing data"],"Organization keeps projects on track.")
H("697.d.9.B",3,"A flowchart for a GIS project shows:","the steps and decisions in the project in order",["only the map colors","only the final grade","random notes"],"Visual organizers plan solutions.")
H("697.d.9.B",4,"A schematic used in a GIS project would best show:","how data flows between tools and layers",["a lunch order","a seating chart","a poster's border"],"Schematics show relationships and flow.")
H("697.d.10.A",3,"A finished map can be published as a printed poster or as a:","digital file such as a PDF or web map",["recipe","soundtrack","calendar notice"],"Maps can be published in print or digital forms.")
H("697.d.10.A",4,"When choosing a publication format for a map, the mapmaker should consider:","the audience and how they will use the map",["the pen color only","the weather only","the file icon only"],"Format follows audience and use.")
H("697.d.10.B",3,"A GIS presentation could include maps, charts and:","graphs that support the findings",["unrelated photos","only the title","blank slides"],"Visuals support the message.")
H("697.d.10.B",4,"In a GIS presentation to a city council, the mapmaker should:","use clear maps and charts that support the main point",["fill slides with dense text only","hide the map","skip the data"],"Clear visuals communicate findings.")
H("697.d.11.A",3,"A reader is confused by a map's colored symbols. The part of the map that explains them is the legend, which tells:","what the symbols and colors on the map mean",["who owns the printer","when school ends","what is for lunch"],"Legends are keys to symbols.")
H("697.d.11.A",4,"Industry-standard legends help GIS users because they:","let different people read maps the same way",["hide the data","remove the scale","delete symbols"],"Standard legends promote consistent interpretation.")
H("697.d.11.B",3,"Which is a common map element?","a scale bar",["a stapler","a lunch tray","a jump rope"],"Scale bars, north arrows and titles are map elements.")
H("697.d.11.B",4,"A north arrow on a map tells the reader:","which direction is north",["the map's price","the printer brand","the paper weight"],"It orients the map.")
