H("698.d.1.D",3,"Using someone's location data without permission raises an ethical issue about:","privacy",["font size","paper weight","screen glare"],"Location data can reveal personal details.")
H("698.d.1.D",4,"A GIS analyst should avoid sharing maps that show:","private home locations of vulnerable people without consent",["a public park","a state boundary","a river's name"],"Ethics protect privacy and safety.")
H("698.d.2.A",3,"Why is teamwork important in a GIS project?","Different members bring different skills and share the workload",["It avoids all planning","It removes the need for data","It hides errors"],"Large projects need collaboration.")
H("698.d.2.A",4,"A GIS project needs a data collector, an analyst and a map designer. This shows the value of:","teamwork with specialized roles",["working alone","skipping tasks","random assignments"],"Roles combine to finish the work.")
H("698.d.2.B",3,"A teammate disagrees about which map colors to use. The best principle for handling it is:","calm conflict resolution through discussion",["ignoring the teammate","yelling","quitting the team"],"Effective teams resolve conflict respectfully.")
H("698.d.2.B",4,"Collaboration on a GIS team includes:","sharing ideas, listening and agreeing on goals",["hiding progress","working in secret","blaming others"],"Collaboration needs communication.")
H("698.d.2.C",3,"A strong team leader:","guides the group and values every member's input",["makes all decisions silently","avoids all work","ignores deadlines"],"Good leaders support the team.")
H("698.d.2.C",4,"A strong team member:","meets deadlines and supports teammates",["blames others","skips meetings","works only for themselves"],"Reliability and support characterize strong members.")
H("698.d.3.A",3,"A camera lens collects and focuses light to form an image. In aerial photography, a longer focal length gives:","a narrower, more magnified view",["a wider view","no image","a dim view only"],"Focal length affects field of view.")
H("698.d.3.A",4,"The camera's film or sensor in aerial photography records:","the focused light from the ground scene",["the pilot's voice","the engine temperature","the fuel level"],"Sensors capture the image.")
H("698.d.3.B",3,"Early aerial photographs were taken from platforms such as:","balloons, kites and pigeons",["submarines","bicycles","trucks"],"Early platforms were simple aircraft and balloons.")
H("698.d.3.B",4,"Aerial photography developed rapidly in wartime because of its value for:","reconnaissance and mapping",["cooking","sports scoring","music"],"Military use pushed the technology forward.")
H("698.d.3.C",3,"A land developer uses aerial photos to:","study a site before building",["bake a cake","write a song","paint a portrait"],"Aerial photos show terrain and features.")
H("698.d.3.C",4,"Aerial photography is used by farmers to:","check crop health across fields",["print recipes","tune pianos","dye fabric"],"It reveals field conditions.")
H("698.d.3.D",3,"A photograph taken with the camera pointing straight down is a:","vertical aerial photograph",["oblique aerial photograph","portrait","panorama only"],"Vertical photos look straight down.")
H("698.d.3.D",4,"An oblique aerial photograph differs from a vertical one because it:","is taken at an angle, showing sides of objects",["is taken straight down","has no horizon","never shows buildings"],"Oblique views show angled perspective.")
H("698.d.3.E",3,"In an aerial photo, long straight dark lines connecting towns are most likely:","roads",["rivers' deltas","clouds","shadows of the moon"],"Roads appear as straight linear features.")
H("698.d.3.E",4,"In an aerial photo, a long dark curved band bordering open water is likely a:","shoreline",["highway overpass","parking lot","airport runway"],"Shorelines mark land-water boundaries.")
H("698.d.4.A",3,"Electromagnetic radiation from the Sun travels through space as:","waves of energy",["sound only","liquid","solid rock"],"EM radiation propagates as waves.")
H("698.d.4.A",4,"When EM energy reaches Earth's surface it can be reflected, absorbed or:","transmitted",["frozen","spoken","printed"],"Matter interacts with energy in these ways.")
H("698.d.4.B",3,"When light bends as it passes from air into water, the wave behavior is:","refraction",["deletion","scaling","pixelation"],"Refraction is bending at a boundary.")
H("698.d.4.B",4,"Light spreading in many directions after hitting small particles in the air is:","scattering",["focusing","freezing","printing"],"Scattering redirects waves.")
H("698.d.4.C",3,"According to thermal radiation laws, hotter objects emit:","more energy at shorter wavelengths",["no energy","only sound","less energy than cold objects"],"Hotter objects radiate more and at shorter wavelengths.")
H("698.d.4.C",4,"All objects above absolute zero emit thermal radiation, so a thermal sensor can detect:","differences in surface temperature",["only colors","only sounds","only smells"],"Thermal sensors read emitted heat.")
H("698.d.4.D",3,"The wave model of light explains behaviors such as:","interference and diffraction",["batteries","paper folding","glue drying"],"Wave behaviors include interference.")
H("698.d.4.D",4,"The particle model of light describes it as streams of:","photons",["atoms of water","grains of sand","raindrops"],"Photons are light particles.")
H("698.d.4.E",3,"A map made from reflected visible light shows how objects look. A thermal image map shows:","how hot or cold surfaces are",["only street names","only borders","only sounds"],"Thermal imagery maps temperature.")
H("698.d.4.E",4,"To tell which parts of a city lose the most heat at night, an analyst would use:","thermal radiation imagery",["a road atlas","a recipe","a calendar"],"Thermal images show heat loss.")
H("698.d.4.F",3,"To map wildfire hot spots through smoke, the better choice is:","thermal imagery",["visible-light photos only","a paper map","a street guide"],"Thermal sensors detect heat through smoke.")
H("698.d.4.F",4,"Choosing between visible and thermal imagery should be based on:","what the project needs to detect",["the file's color","the printer brand","the desk's size"],"Match sensor to purpose.")
H("698.d.5.A",3,"Passive microwave remote sensing measures:","naturally emitted microwave energy",["its own transmitted pulses","sound waves","visible paint"],"Passive systems detect natural energy.")
H("698.d.5.A",4,"Active microwave systems such as radar differ because they:","send out their own signal and measure the return",["only wait for the sun","use no energy","record nothing"],"Active sensors transmit pulses.")
H("698.d.5.B",3,"In radar imagery, a rough surface generally appears:","brighter because it scatters more energy back",["darker always","invisible","blue only"],"Roughness increases backscatter.")
H("698.d.5.B",4,"Wet soil usually returns a stronger radar signal than dry soil because of:","its higher moisture content",["its lower moisture","its color","its smell"],"Moisture changes the radar response.")
H("698.d.5.C",3,"An analyst studying a radar image of a coastline can often tell:","water from land by differences in brightness",["the day's menu","the user's password","the owner's name"],"Smooth water and rough land differ in radar returns.")
H("698.d.5.C",4,"A detailed radar image analysis of a flood would compare:","images before and after the event to find changes",["a single blank page","only the title","music playlists"],"Change detection reveals flooding.")
H("698.d.6.A",3,"Raster-based GIS software stores data as:","a grid of cells with values",["only lines","only text","paper sheets"],"Rasters are cell grids.")
H("698.d.6.A",4,"Using raster software to compute the average elevation of cells within a watershed is an example of:","raster analysis",["word counting","file deleting","font choosing"],"Cell-based math is raster analysis.")
H("698.d.6.B",3,"Re-projecting a downloaded image means:","changing it to match the map's coordinate system",["deleting it","printing it twice","renaming only"],"Layers must share a projection.")
H("698.d.6.B",4,"If two layers appear in different places even though they cover the same area, the likely cause is:","mismatched projections or coordinate systems",["a dirty screen","a loose cable","a low battery"],"Projection mismatch shifts layers.")
H("698.d.6.C",3,"A device in an aircraft that detects reflected energy from the ground is:","remote sensing equipment",["a printer","a cookbook","a clock"],"Sensors on platforms collect imagery.")
H("698.d.6.C",4,"GPS differs from remote sensing because GPS:","determines a position from satellite signals",["captures images from far away","measures soil moisture only","records weather only"],"GPS locates positions; remote sensing images.")
H("698.d.6.D",3,"A handheld GPS device measures:","position, distance and elevation",["only temperature","only sound","only time zones"],"Handhelds provide basic measurements.")
H("698.d.6.D",4,"To measure the length of a trail with a handheld GPS, a technician:","records a track while walking the trail",["draws it from memory","skips recording","guesses the distance"],"Tracks record paths.")
H("698.d.6.E",3,"A drone differs from a satellite because a drone:","can be flown at low altitude for fine detail on demand",["orbits the Earth forever","cannot carry sensors","needs no pilot rules"],"Drones give flexible, high-resolution coverage.")
H("698.d.6.E",4,"A limitation of unmanned aerial sensing is:","weather, battery life and flight rules limiting coverage",["unlimited flight time","no sensors","worldwide coverage at once"],"Drones have operating limits.")
H("698.d.7.A",3,"A GIS investigation starts with:","asking a question and forming a hypothesis",["printing the map","closing the file","choosing a font"],"Investigations begin with questions.")
H("698.d.7.A",4,"A well-planned GIS investigation includes:","the question, needed data, methods and a schedule",["only a title","a random guess","no steps"],"Plans guide efficient work.")
H("698.d.7.B",3,"A student collects GIS data by recording locations of storm drains with GPS. This is:","data collection",["data deletion","map framing","report printing"],"Fieldwork gathers spatial data.")
H("698.d.7.B",4,"Good GIS data collection requires that each record has:","accurate location and clear attribute information",["a missing location","no description","a random name"],"Complete records are usable.")
H("698.d.7.C",3,"After collecting data, the analyst organizes it, analyzes it and:","draws conclusions and may predict trends",["throws it away","hides it","renames it as unknown"],"Analysis leads to inferences.")
H("698.d.7.C",4,"Spotting that crime reports increase each summer and forecasting next year's pattern is:","predicting a trend from GIS data",["a printing error","a projection change","a file backup"],"Trends support predictions.")
H("698.d.7.D",3,"When reporting results, an analyst should use:","correct GIS vocabulary and supporting maps",["slang only","no evidence","random terms"],"Clear communication needs vocabulary and visuals.")
H("698.d.7.D",4,"A valid conclusion in a GIS report is one that:","is supported by the data and maps shown",["is only an opinion","ignores the data","contradicts the maps"],"Conclusions follow evidence.")
H("698.d.8.A",3,"To evaluate a local flooding problem, a team first identifies:","the problem and the data needed",["the weather forecast only","the colors of the map","the file size"],"Define the problem, then gather data.")
H("698.d.8.A",4,"For a local erosion project, necessary data might include:","elevation, soil and land cover layers",["music files","recipes","sports scores"],"Relevant layers support analysis.")
H("698.d.8.B",3,"A project plan for a GIS study should include:","tasks and a schedule for completing them",["no dates","only a title","random steps"],"Plans need tasks and timeline.")
H("698.d.8.B",4,"A schedule helps a GIS team by:","showing what must be done and when",["hiding the steps","removing deadlines","skipping tasks"],"Schedules keep work on track.")
H("698.d.8.C",3,"A team uses satellite images to create a map of the problem area. This is:","creating a GIS map from remote sensing images",["deleting layers","writing a recipe","printing a blank sheet"],"Imagery supports maps.")
H("698.d.8.C",4,"When creating a problem map, the team should include:","a title, legend, scale and north arrow",["only a border","only a photo","no labels"],"Map elements aid interpretation.")
H("698.d.8.D",3,"Looking at map features to find which areas are most at risk is:","evaluating map features to identify solutions",["deleting layers","renaming layers","changing fonts"],"Evaluation points to solutions.")
H("698.d.8.D",4,"If a map shows runoff collecting in one low area, a likely solution to evaluate is:","adding drainage or retention there",["ignoring the area","building in the low area","removing the map"],"Evidence guides solutions.")
H("698.d.8.E",3,"Using raster GIS to model how water flows over terrain helps to:","develop solutions to reduce flooding",["print posters","create passwords","edit audio"],"Models support solution design.")
H("698.d.8.E",4,"A raster analysis that finds the steepest paths of runoff supports solving problems by:","showing where to place controls",["hiding the map","deleting the data","changing the title"],"Analysis locates intervention points.")
H("698.d.8.F",3,"At the end of a project, findings are shared in a:","final report or poster",["blank page","random note","hidden file"],"Reports communicate results.")
H("698.d.8.F",4,"A final report on a local problem should present:","the data, analysis, maps and recommended solution",["only the cover","only a single number","only jokes"],"Reports tell the complete story.")

# ---- 699 Spatial Technology / Remote Sensing ----
H("699.d.1.A",3,"A student who enjoys drones and maps might consider a career as a:","remote sensing technician",["pastry chef","court reporter","florist"],"Remote sensing careers use sensors and imagery.")
H("699.d.1.A",4,"Which employer commonly hires people trained in spatial technology and remote sensing?","a utility company monitoring its power lines",["a toy store","a movie theater","a hair salon"],"Utilities map and inspect infrastructure.")
H("699.d.1.B",3,"A student sits in with a surveyor for a day to see the job. This is:","job shadowing",["a final test","a loan","a license"],"Shadowing exposes students to real work.")
H("699.d.1.B",4,"Another career preparation experience is:","an internship at an engineering firm",["a long vacation","a video game","a lunch break"],"Internships provide practice.")
H("699.d.1.C",3,"Certifications help a spatial technology worker by:","proving their skills to employers",["replacing all training","ending the career","closing a file"],"Certifications signal competence.")
H("699.d.1.C",4,"Which would be an industry certification for a drone operator?","a Part 107 remote pilot certificate",["a library card","a swim badge","a gym pass"],"Commercial drone work requires an FAA certificate.")
H("699.d.1.D",3,"Flying a drone over a private backyard and recording it raises a concern about:","privacy",["gravity","batteries","paper"],"Imagery can invade privacy.")
H("699.d.1.D",4,"An ethical remote sensing professional should:","follow laws and respect people's privacy",["ignore all rules","record anyone","sell private images"],"Ethics and legality guide the work.")
H("699.d.2.A",3,"The Mercator projection keeps the correct:","shape and direction of small areas, stretching land near the poles",["size of all countries","temperature of oceans","speed of ships"],"Mercator preserves direction but distorts area at high latitudes.")
H("699.d.2.A",4,"On a Mercator map, Greenland appears much larger than it really is because:","the projection stretches areas near the poles",["Greenland has grown","maps are wrong by law","the scale is 1:1"],"Area distortion increases with latitude.")
H("699.d.2.B",3,"The Albers conic projection is often used for maps of:","mid-latitude regions like the continental United States",["the North Pole only","the Moon","a single room"],"Albers suits east-west mid-latitude areas.")
H("699.d.2.B",4,"The Albers conic projection is useful for statistics maps because it:","preserves area",["preserves all directions","has no distortion","shows no borders"],"Equal-area projections suit comparisons.")
H("699.d.2.C",3,"Different map projections were developed because:","no flat map can show the curved Earth without some distortion",["the Earth is flat","maps are free","ink is cheap"],"Every projection compromises.")
H("699.d.2.C",4,"A mapmaker picks a projection to match the map's:","purpose, such as navigation or area comparison",["paper color","title length","printer"],"Purpose guides projection choice.")
H("699.d.3.A",3,"In GPS terms, a waypoint is:","a saved location with coordinates",["a battery","a satellite's name","a map border"],"Waypoints are stored positions.")
H("699.d.3.A",4,"A recorded line of positions showing the path you traveled is a:","track",["legend","scale","title"],"Tracks record movement.")
H("699.d.3.B",3,"A GPS receiver gets its position by using signals from:","satellites",["radio towers only","street signs","wall clocks"],"GPS uses satellite signals.")
H("699.d.3.B",4,"The antenna of a GPS receiver should be:","oriented with a clear view of the sky",["wrapped in foil","buried underground","placed inside a drawer"],"Open sky improves reception.")
H("699.d.3.C",3,"Mapping fire hydrant locations with GPS helps a city to:","find and maintain them for emergencies",["bake bread","write songs","paint murals"],"Asset mapping aids public safety.")
H("699.d.3.C",4,"Utility crews use GPS coordinates to:","locate buried pipes and poles",["design logos","create playlists","write novels"],"Coordinates guide field work.")
H("699.d.3.D",3,"A smartphone's built-in GPS is usually:","less accurate than a survey-grade receiver",["more accurate than any receiver","unable to find locations","free of satellites"],"Consumer devices have larger errors.")
H("699.d.3.D",4,"A surveyor needs centimeter-level accuracy, so they use:","a high-precision survey-grade GPS receiver",["a phone with no signal","a paper map","a hand-drawn sketch"],"Specialized receivers give higher accuracy.")
H("699.d.4.A",3,"A satellite is a type of:","aerial or space remote sensing platform",["underwater platform","kitchen appliance","chair"],"Satellites carry sensors from orbit.")
H("699.d.4.A",4,"An underwater vehicle that maps the seafloor is a:","submersible remote sensing platform",["weather balloon","satellite","airplane"],"Submersibles operate underwater.")
H("699.d.4.B",3,"To map a small construction site often, the best platform is probably:","a drone",["a deep space probe","a weather satellite","a submarine"],"Drones give frequent, detailed coverage.")
H("699.d.4.B",4,"The best platform for mapping an entire continent's vegetation is:","a satellite",["a handheld camera","a kite","a backyard drone"],"Satellites cover large areas.")
H("699.d.4.C",3,"A camera sensor on a drone captures:","visible-light photographs",["radio music","soil by touch","smells"],"Cameras record visible light.")
H("699.d.4.C",4,"LiDAR is a sensing system that uses:","laser pulses to measure distances",["sound recording","paper drawings","heat blankets"],"LiDAR measures distance with lasers.")
H("699.d.4.D",3,"To map cave interiors where GPS signals can't reach, a team might choose:","an unmanned ground or aerial platform with onboard sensors",["a satellite photo","a paper atlas","a weather report"],"Platforms must fit conditions.")
H("699.d.4.D",4,"A team compares drones and satellites for monthly crop checks over a small farm. The drone is often chosen because it offers:","higher detail and flexible timing",["worldwide coverage","orbit access","no battery needs"],"Drones suit small, frequent surveys.")
H("699.d.5.A",3,"After analyzing GIS data, a team notices gaps in the data. This is:","a potential problem to evaluate",["a perfect result","an end to the project","a printer error"],"Gaps affect reliability.")
H("699.d.5.A",4,"When findings from GIS data conflict, an analyst should:","check data quality and methods",["delete the results","ignore the conflict","guess"],"Evaluate sources of error.")
H("699.d.5.B",3,"A model that shows how land use changes the flow of runoff is a:","model representing GIS data",["recipe","poster only","logo"],"Models represent real data.")
H("699.d.5.B",4,"Modeling collected GIS data helps users to:","test scenarios and see likely outcomes",["avoid data","hide the project","skip analysis"],"Models support what-if questions.")
H("699.d.5.C",3,"A raster stores a landscape as:","a grid of cells, each with a value",["a list of sentences","a single point","a paragraph"],"Raster data is cell-based.")
H("699.d.5.C",4,"Querying a raster to find all cells with slopes above 20 degrees selects:","the cells that meet the slope condition",["every cell","no cells","only the borders"],"Queries filter cell values.")
H("699.d.5.D",3,"Measuring how far each school is from the nearest fire station is a:","distance analysis",["font change","file rename","slide design"],"Distance analysis measures separation.")
H("699.d.5.D",4,"A proximity analysis of clinics and neighborhoods can show:","which areas are far from health services",["only the road names","the printer model","a lunch menu"],"Proximity identifies underserved areas.")
H("699.d.6.A",3,"Census data about population and income is a source of:","geospatial socioeconomic data",["weather forecasts only","music charts","recipes"],"Census data describes communities.")
H("699.d.6.A",4,"Before mapping income data by neighborhood, a team should organize it:","with matching geographic identifiers",["with random labels","without a source","by color only"],"Joins need matching geography codes.")
H("699.d.6.B",3,"A map shaded only to display average rainfall across a state is an example of a thematic map, which focuses on:","one topic such as population density across an area",["every topic at once","no data","only a legend"],"Thematic maps focus on a theme.")
H("699.d.6.B",4,"Planning a thematic map includes choosing the theme, the data classes and:","the colors and legend",["a random font","no title","a blank page"],"Design decisions follow the theme.")
H("699.d.6.C",3,"Turning a flat map into a 3D view with building heights helps to:","show feature heights and terrain visually",["hide the data","delete layers","print less"],"3D shows vertical dimension.")
H("699.d.6.C",4,"A 3D map of a city can demonstrate:","how tall buildings are relative to each other",["the printer's age","the user's name","a battery's size"],"Height data becomes visible in 3D.")
H("699.d.6.D",3,"After mapping income by area, a student draws a conclusion and:","justifies it with the map and data",["makes it up","hides the map","ignores the data"],"Conclusions need support.")
H("699.d.6.D",4,"A justified conclusion about socioeconomic patterns should:","cite the data and avoid unsupported claims",["rely only on opinions","use no maps","skip the sources"],"Evidence-based interpretation.")
H("699.d.7.A",3,"Collecting the boundary of a school campus with GPS requires:","walking the edge and recording points",["staying home","drawing from memory","skipping the edge"],"Boundaries are captured by tracing.")
H("699.d.7.A",4,"Using an unmanned system to map a campus, the team must also follow:","safety and flight regulations",["no rules","only personal preference","club rules only"],"Drone use is regulated.")
H("699.d.7.B",3,"A community near a river may face a hardship such as:","flooding",["no sunsets","too many stars","few clouds"],"Location affects hazards.")
H("699.d.7.B",4,"A town with a nearby lake and farmland benefits from resources like:","water and fertile soil",["no resources","only shadows","only paper"],"Location shapes resources.")
H("699.d.7.C",3,"A campus map should show buildings, facilities and:","adjacent streets",["only the sky","nothing else","random doodles"],"Context locates the site.")
H("699.d.7.C",4,"A good facility map includes a legend that explains:","the symbols for buildings and features",["the weather","the lunch menu","the phone number"],"Legends explain symbols.")
H("699.d.7.D",3,"A map categorizing restrooms, entrances and parking helps visitors:","find what they need",["avoid the building","lose the way","skip reading"],"Categories organize features.")
H("699.d.7.D",4,"Adding an accessibility category to a facility map helps:","users find ramps and accessible entrances",["no one","only the designer","only the printer"],"Accessibility information serves users.")
H("699.d.8.A",3,"A spatial technology portfolio includes:","evidence of skills such as maps, projects and certificates",["only a blank folder","only jokes","only passwords"],"Portfolios document attainments.")
H("699.d.8.A",4,"Items that belong in a portfolio of spatial work include:","completed maps, project reports and certifications",["unfinished doodles","unrelated photos","spam emails"],"Include evidence of achievement.")
H("699.d.8.B",3,"Presenting a portfolio to stakeholders is a chance to:","explain your skills and projects",["hide your work","avoid questions","skip the audience"],"Presenting shares accomplishments.")
H("699.d.8.B",4,"During a portfolio presentation, the student earns the most credibility by:","tell the story of the projects and answer questions",["read silently","avoid eye contact","leave early"],"Clear explanation builds credibility.")

